LOG pikachu-quick-attack-two-point-qa

# Direct gameplay fixture: boot 1-1, launch into open air, then aim the first
# Quick Attack zip right and the second zip up.  The two turns are held across
# the exact source input samples so this exercises the public NES mapping, the
# controller's 20-frame aim, the 5-frame first zip, and the changed-direction
# second-zip window—not an injected controller harness state.
WAIT 60
HOLD START
WAIT 6
RELEASE START
WAIT_RAM8 000E 08
WAIT 30

# Start from ordinary ground: the zip itself owns its takeoff, and this keeps
# the neutral-UP first point below the HUD so the second Right point is visible.
HOLD UP
HOLD B
WAIT 2
RELEASE B
RELEASE UP

# First aim: neutral is sampled at source frame 20 and must default UP.
WAIT 17
SCREENSHOT C:/temp/pikachu_quick_two_point_aim1.png
WAIT 2
SCREENSHOT C:/temp/pikachu_quick_two_point_zip1.png
WAIT 4

# Second aim: right, a 90-degree change. Hold it through the source end-script
# decision rather than requiring a frame-perfect tap.
HOLD RIGHT
SCREENSHOT C:/temp/pikachu_quick_two_point_aim2.png
WAIT 12
SCREENSHOT C:/temp/pikachu_quick_two_point_zip2.png
WAIT 5
RELEASE RIGHT
SCREENSHOT C:/temp/pikachu_quick_two_point_recovery.png
WAIT 24

# The source end-script decides on the ninth wait tick; retain Right one extra
# host frame so screenshot/UI command scheduling cannot release it early.
# Any forced scripted handoff here is a host-coupling regression.
ASSERT_RAM8 000E 08
DUMP_RAM 0060 40
DUMP_RAM 00B0 30
EXIT 0
